Ben Rosengart <ben+rgrn@panix.com> wrote:
> If I throw a missile weapon, I probably want to pick it up when I
> see it again.  Yay for autopickup.

You mean: Yay for pickup_thrown. :-)

> But if I throw anything else, I'm probably just getting it out of
> the way.

If pickup_thrown is true and autopickup is also true, evertyhing you
throw will be picked up, regardless if it matches pickup_types or not.

If pickup_dropped is false and you drop something it won't be picked
up even if it matches pickup_types.

But pickup_types must be set to something for this to work. If you
don't ever want to pickup else than thrown stuff, set pickup_types to
iron chains. They are so rare it won't matter.

> Suggestion: create an option to autopickup missile weapons only.

If the different pickup_* options are not fine-grained enough for you,
you could use autopickup exceptions as TJR suggested. But they need to
be enabled at compile time. I have again forgotten to enable them per
default in this release.

